    "title": "Search for the $K_L \\!\\to\\! \\pi^0 \\nu \\overline{\\nu}$ and $K_L \\!\\to\\! \\pi^0 X^0$ decays at the J-PARC KOTO experiment",
    "arxiv": "1810.09655v2 [hep-ex]",
    "time": "2019-02-26",
    "abstract": "A search for the rare decay $K_L \\to \\pi^0 \\nu \\bar{\\nu}$ was performed. With the data collected in 2015, corresponding to $2.2 \\times 10^{19}$ protons on target, a single event was observed with an expected background of $0.42 \\pm 0.18$ events. An upper limit on the branching ratio of $\\mathcal{B}(K_L \\to \\pi^0 \\nu \\bar{\\nu}) < 4.9 \\times 10^{-9}$ at the 90% confidence level was obtained. The single event sensitivity was $(1.30 \\pm 0.01_{\\rm stat} \\pm 0.14_{\\rm syst}) \\times 10^{-9}$.",
